<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Githeri components and cost</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>A school cook mixes maize and beans in the ratio \({@a@} : {@b@}\) by mass to make \({@N@}\) kg of githeri mix. Maize costs Ksh \({@p1@}\) a kilogram and beans Ksh \({@p2@}\) a kilogram.</p><p>(a) What mass of beans is used? Give your answer exactly or correct to 1 decimal place.</p><p>[[input:ans1]] kg [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p><p>(b) What does 1 kg of the mix cost, to the nearest shilling?</p><p>Ksh [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) There are \({@a@} + {@b@} = {@a+b@}\) parts, so one part is \({@N@} \div {@a+b@} = {@dd(N/(a+b))@}\) kg. Beans: \({@b@} \times {@dd(N/(a+b))@} = {@dd(Bm)@}\) kg (and maize \({@dd(Mz)@}\) kg).</p><p>(b) The whole mix costs \({@dd(Mz)@} \times {@p1@} + {@dd(Bm)@} \times {@p2@} = {@ksh(tc)@}\) shillings for \({@N@}\) kg, so 1 kg costs \({@ksh(tc)@} \div {@N@} [[if test="is(integerp(100*cc))"]]= {@ksh(cc)@}[[else]]\approx {@ksh(cc)@}[[/if]]\), that is Ksh \({@floor(cc+1/2)@}\) to the nearest shilling.</p><p>The cost of a mixture leans towards the ingredient you use more of. More maize than beans is used, so the cost is nearer the maize price than the mean, Ksh \({@dd(mn)@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[kgrp(n) := block([s, out, k], s: string(n), k: slength(s), if k < 5 then s else (out: "", while k > 3 do (out: sconcat("\\,", substring(s, k-2, k+1), out), k: k-3), sconcat(substring(s, 1, k+1), out)));
ksh(v) := block([c, w, f], c: floor(100*v+1/2), w: floor(c/100), f: c-100*w, if f = 0 then kgrp(w) else sconcat(kgrp(w), ".", if f < 10 then "0" else "", string(f)));
dd(v) := if integerp(v) then v else if integerp(10*v) then dispdp(float(v),1) else if integerp(100*v) then dispdp(float(v),2) else if integerp(1000*v) then dispdp(float(v),3) else dispdp(float(v),4);
fr(v) := if integerp(v) then string(v) else sconcat("\\frac{", string(num(v)), "}{", string(denom(v)), "}");
r1(v) := floor(10*v+1/2)/10;
ix: 1+rand(10);
/* Design: components of a mixture from a ratio, then its cost. Source: adapted from SMP GCSE Foundation 1, Chapter 23, Section E; the costing part is original. [a, b, N, p1, p2]: maize : beans = a : b, N kg in all, prices a kg. Curated list, one seed per entry. */
L: [[3,2,40,50,150],[5,2,42,52,136],[7,4,55,54,138],[7,5,60,58,146],[7,3,60,50,140],[5,4,45,56,155],[7,2,63,48,165],[9,4,65,60,151],[8,3,44,51,150],[3,2,75,62,132]];
E: L[ix];
a: E[1]; b: E[2]; N: E[3]; p1: E[4]; p2: E[5];
Mz: N*a/(a+b);
Bm: N*b/(a+b);
cc: (a*p1+b*p2)/(a+b);
st: a*p1+b*p2;
tc: Mz*p1+Bm*p2;
/* diagnostics */
Nba: N*b/a;
mn: (p1+p2)/2;
sw: (b*p1+a*p2)/(a+b);
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
