  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Compound Proportions: components and cost of a mixture</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 1.3 / Essential 1.2 (C d; E e): Find the mass of one component of a mixture from a ratio, and the cost of 1 kg of the mixture.</p><p id="edition">Core and Essential</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 23 (Ratio and proportion), Section E of Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP GCSE Mathematics: Foundation 1 for AQA, Edexcel and OCR two-tier GCSE mathematics, Cambridge University Press, 2006: components of a mixture from a ratio, with new ratios and a Kenyan githeri context; costing the mixture is new.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core and Essential Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
